.SH NAME
cd \- change working directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cd
.I directory
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Directory
becomes the new working directory.
The process must have execute (search) permission in
.IR directory .
.PP
\fBCd\fR is recognized and executed by the shell.
A new process is created to execute each command, and
.B cd
would be ineffective if it were written as a normal command.
.SH SEE ALSO
csh(1), pwd(1), sh(1), chdir(2).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual
